From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coaxk <juddhowie@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 12:56:39 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] 0048: advertise the effective SKIP_IF_AUDIO_LANGUAGES
 list, and stop the override log claiming a bypass

subarr cannot currently decide whether forwarding a user-verified audio language
is safe, because audio_language_override SUBSTITUTES that language into the skip
check rather than bypassing it:

    if audio_language_override is not None:
        audio_langs = [audio_language_override]
    ...
    if any(lang in skip_audio_languages for lang in audio_langs):
        return True   # skip

Declaring en to an install that sets SKIP_IF_AUDIO_LANGUAGES=eng therefore SKIPS
the file, which is the opposite of what the verifying user wanted. subarr had no
way to tell such an install apart from one that skips nothing, so it withheld
English overrides from everyone and silently discarded a verification the user
had explicitly made. Reported as coaxk/subarr#498 by IdahoRC.

The effective list is now advertised in the /queue capabilities block as
2-letter ISO-639-1 codes, empty when unset. Emitted as codes rather than as a
boolean so subarr can answer the same question for any target language later,
not just English. Verified serialisation: unset gives [], eng gives ['en'],
eng|jpn gives ['en','ja'], and an unparseable code is filtered rather than
emitting a null into the list.

The log line is also corrected. It claimed the override will bypass the
SKIP_IF_AUDIO_LANGUAGES check. It never did. It replaces the value that check
reads, and that wording is precisely what led the reporter to conclude the
mechanism was safe for English.
---
 subgen.py | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/subgen.py b/subgen.py
index 6da0584..f5c08d9 100644
--- a/subgen.py
+++ b/subgen.py
@@ -828,6 +828,20 @@ def queue_status():
         "subarr_subgen_release_tag": subarr_subgen_release_tag,
         "capabilities": {
             "audio_language_override": True,
+            # [v4.28 PATCH #498] The EFFECTIVE SKIP_IF_AUDIO_LANGUAGES list, as
+            # 2-letter ISO-639-1 codes ([] when unset). subarr needs to see this
+            # because audio_language_override SUBSTITUTES the declared language
+            # into the skip check rather than bypassing it: forwarding a verified
+            # 'en' to an install that skips English audio makes the file SKIP
+            # instead of transcribe, which is the opposite of the user's intent.
+            # Without this list subarr cannot tell such an install apart from one
+            # that skips nothing, so it had to withhold English overrides from
+            # everybody -- discarding a verification the user had explicitly made
+            # (coaxk/subarr#498). Emitted as codes rather than a bool so subarr
+            # can answer the same question for any target language later.
+            "skip_audio_languages": [
+                c for c in (lc.to_iso_639_1() for lc in skip_audio_languages) if c
+            ],
             # [PATCH 0027 / #17] detect_language_robust accepts ?track=N (0-based
             # audio stream) so subarr can language-detect a specific non-default
             # track -- gates the Review "re-run on track N" confirmation UI.
@@ -3496,7 +3510,10 @@ def transcribe_existing(transcribe_folders, forceLanguage : LanguageCode | None
     logging.info(f"Starting to search folders to see if we need to create subtitles (Reverse={reverse}).")
     if audio_language_override is not None:
         logging.info(f"[v4.3 PATCH] audio_language_override={audio_language_override.to_name()} — "
-                     f"will bypass SKIP_IF_AUDIO_LANGUAGES check + seed Whisper source.")
+                     f"REPLACES the detected audio language for the "
+                     f"SKIP_IF_AUDIO_LANGUAGES check (it does NOT bypass that "
+                     f"check, so declaring a skipped language will skip the file) "
+                     f"+ seeds the Whisper source language.")
     logging.debug("The folders are:")
 
     # [v4.1 PATCH] Structured dispatch counts for /batch return.
